{"id":"word:hebrew:H1366","type":"word","title":"גְּבוּל","subtitle":"H1366 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, a cord (as twisted ), i.e. (by implication) a boundary ; by extension the territory inclosed","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to גְּבוּל (H1366) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 241 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"גְּבוּל (gᵉbûwl) means properly, a cord (as twisted ), i.e. (by implication) a boundary ; by extension the territory inclosed First listed occurrence: 1Chr 4 10."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"גְּבוּל","transliteration":"gᵉbûwl","pronunciation":"gheb-ool'","strong":"H1366","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1366","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["גְּב֣וּל","גְּב֥וּל","הַ/גְּבוּל֙","גְּב֖וּל","הַ/גְּב֜וּל"],"morphs":[["HNcmsc",93],["HTd/Ncmsa",48],["HNcmsc/Sp3mp",15],["HR/Ncmsc",12],["HC/Ncmsa",11],["HNcmsc/Sp2ms",11],["HNcmsa",7],["HC/Ncmsc",7],["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",6],["HNcmsc/Sp3fs",5]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, a cord (as twisted ), i.e. (by implication) a boundary ; by extension the territory inclosed","usage":"border, bound, coast, × great, landmark, limit, quarter, space.","full":"H1366. gebul (ה)גבול Josh 15:47 Kt; read הַגָּדוֺל Vrss. Manuscripts compare 15:12 . גבח (only in following derivatives found in P; compare also Late Hebrew גִּבֵּחַ , giant ). גְּבוּל 240 noun masculine Num 34:3 border, boundary, territory (Late Hebrew id. , Punic gubulim (plural, Plaut Poen. i. 9 ) — גָּבוּל Gen 10:19 168t. + Josh 15:47 Kt (but read Qr גָּדוֺל ); גְּבֻל Num 21:13 9 t.; (both, in absolute & construct, e.g. absolute 22:36 ; 34:8 , construct Gen 10:19 ; 2Sam 21:5 ); suffix גְּבוּלִי 1Chr 4:10 , גְּבוּלְךָ Exodus 7:27, גְבֻלְךָ Exod 23:31 3 t., etc.; plural (8 t.) only suffix גְּבוּלֶיךָ Jer 15:13 ; 17:3 , etc.; &#8212; 1 border, boundary , a. of a land or people : Canaanites Gen 10:19 (J), Edom Num 20:23 ; Josh 15:1 , 21 (all P) compare Obadiah 7, Amorites Num 21:13 (E) Josh 13:4 (D) compare 12:5 (D) Judg 1:36 , Moab Num 21:13 , 15 ; 22:36 (E) 33:44 (P) Deut 2:18 ; Judg 11:18 (twice in verse); 2Kin 3:21 ; Isa 15:8 , Ammon Num 21:24 (E) Deut 3:16 ; Josh 12:2 ; 13:10 (all D) Amos 1:3 , Bashan Josh 12:4 (D), Egypt 1Kin 5:1 2Chr 9:26 ; Isa 19:19 ; especially of promised land Exod 23:31 ; 34:24 (JE) Num 34:3 13 t. Numbers 34 (all P) Deut 11:24 ; 12:20 ; 16:4 ; Josh 1:4 (D), compare Ezek 45:1 ; 10 t. Ezekiel 45-48; also of Israel 2Kin 14:25 ; Amos 6:2 ; Mal 1:5 . b. boundary of smaller divisions, e.g. Geshurites Deut 3:14 ; Josh 12:5 ; 13:11 (all D), compare 16:2-3 ,(J) 19:12 (P); especially of tribes of Israel Deut 3:16-17 , Josh 13:30 (all D) 13:16 60t. Joshua 13-19 (P); — 15:47 read גדול see above; 22:25 (P) & 17:8 ; 18:11 ; 24:30 (JE), compare 1Chr 6:39 ; 6:51 ; 2Chr 11:13 ; Ezek 48:1 15 t. Ezekiel 48 (including 48:22 ; 48:22 q. strike out Co); — in 1Sam 13:18 read for ᵐ5 הַגֶּבַע גְּבוּל, We Dr. c. boundary of territory belonging to an individual, — of field, piece of ground, etc. Gen 23:17 (P) Deut 19:14 ; 27:17 ; Josh 24:30 (E) = Judg 2:9 ; 1Chr 4:10 ; Prov 15:25 ; 22:28 ; 23:10 ; Hosea 5:10 . d. border of stream Num 22:36 . e. limit to waters of deep Psa 104:9 compare Jer 5:22 . f. a concrete object marking limit , ( α ) barrier in Ezekiel's temple Ezek 40:12 (strike out ᵑ6 ᵐ5 Co) 40:12 ; ( β ) border of altar 43:13 , 17 , 20 ; ( γ ) surrounding wall of restored Zion Isa 54:12 (so ᵐ5 Ew Kn Che; De Brd territory , Di undecided). 2 territory (enclosed within boundary), a. of land or people Gen 47:21 (J) Exodus 7:27 (P) Exod 10:4 , 14 (|| ארץ ) 10:19 ; 13:7 (all J), Num 20:16-17 , 21 ; 21:22 (E; || ארץ ) = Judg 11:20 ; Num 21:23 (E) Deut 2:4 ; 19:3 ( ׳גּ אַרְצְךָ ) 19:8 ; 28:40 ; Josh 18:5 (twice in verse) (E) Judg 11:22 ; 19:29 ; 2Sam 21:5 ; 1Kin 1:3 ; 2Kin 10:32 ; 1Chr 21:12 (|| ארץ ) Psa 105:31 (= ארץ in || Ezek 8:16-17 ,) Ezekiel 8:33; Ezek 147:14; Jer 31:17 ; Ezek 11:10-11 , Joel 4:6; Zeph 2:8 . b. territory of a city (or limit of such territory) Num 35:26-27 , Josh 13:26 ; Judg 1:18 (3 t. in verse); Ezek 47:16 (twice in verse); 47:17 (twice in verse) (strike out ᵐ5 Co) 48:1 ; Amos 6:2 . c. territory about Ezekiel's temple Ezek 43:12 . d. plural in like sense (only use of plural), of land Micah 5:5 ; Isa 60:18 (|| ארץ ) Jer 15:13 ; 17:13 , of city 1Sam 5:6 ; 2Kin 15:16 ; 18:8 ; so Ezek 27:4 of Tyre. e. figurative territory (region) of darkness Job 38:20 ; territory of wickedness Mal 1:4 (of Edom); territory of his holiness Psa 78:54 (of Canaan).","rootNote":"or גְּבֻל ; (shortened) from 1379 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 4 10","keyReferences":["1Chr 4 10","1Chr 6 39","1Chr 6 51","1Chr 21 12","1Kgs 1 3","1Kgs 5 1","1Sam 5 6","1Sam 6 9"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":241,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 4 10","book":"1Chr","chapter":4,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גְּבוּלִ/י֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp1cs"},{"reference":"1Chr 6 39","book":"1Chr","chapter":6,"verse":39,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בִּ/גְבוּלָ֑/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsc/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"1Chr 6 51","book":"1Chr","chapter":6,"verse":51,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גְבוּלָ֔/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"1Chr 21 12","book":"1Chr","chapter":21,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גְּב֣וּל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 3","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גְּב֣וּל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 5 1","book":"1Kgs","chapter":5,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גְּב֣וּל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Sam 5 6","book":"1Sam","chapter":5,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גְּבוּלֶֽי/הָ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmpc/Sp3fs"},{"refere